spec: specs/codecs.md, a new section — BACKLOG "resilience" / microservices-next

why: the last cheap gap of the microservices audit. Two services
  share a Schema-encoded message; when one side's case class changes,
  nothing today ANSWERS whether the other side can still read it. The
  decode rules are stated (absent optional, declared default, damage
  is data) but only exercised one value at a time. Schema is a VALUE,
  so the check is a fold over two of them — no Pact, no broker.

what: okay-codec Compat: compare(old, new) → Vector[Change] with a
  verdict per direction (a new reader over old bytes, an old reader
  over new bytes), the rules read off the decoder's own behaviour;
  Compat.check(old, new, Mode) for a test to assert; a printable
  report. Docs: docs/modules/okay-codec.md section, spec section.

next: spec section, code, tests, docs, gate, land
